\f0\fs48 \cf0 Readme
\f1\fs24 \
\
This dataset contains identified Compound Hot-Dry-Windy events for 3108 counties across Contiguous United States.\
\
Files in this dataset use the suffix _xxx to denote the severity level (occurrence rate related to a baseline period of 1980-1999) used to identify the events:\
\

\f2\b Suffix   Occurrence Rate
\f1\b0 \
005        5 per thousand    \
010       10 per thousand\
050       50 per thousand\
\

\f2\b\fs28 File Description
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f2\b 1. Spatial Reference\

\f1\b0 Filename: county.shapefile\
Description: A \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 geospatial vector file containing the boundaries of 3,108 counties in the CONUS.\
Key Identifier: 
\f3\i\b GEOID
\f1\i0\b0  The unique code for each county. This serves as the primary index for linking data in the 
\f4\i .npy 
\f1\i0 and 
\f4\i .csv
\f1\i0  files.\
\

\f2\b 2. Event Dates\

\f1\b0 Filename: CHDW_Events_xxx.npy\
Description: Contains the specific calendar dates where a CHDW event was identified for each county\
\

\f2\b 3.Threshold Information\

\f1\b0 Filename: CHDW_Events_xxx.csv\
Description: Contains the specific physical threshold values and percentile thresholds used to define the extreme events.\

